PianoKeyboard is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE). What it takes from other work, and from where:

UniXNU-sheng (unixnu-research/UniXNU-sheng, main 00ba90984e831e4c6ce30ec3d8a56e6434e9f1af), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/Wn8030.c (sha256 40beab9c2287187e1f62263fba83ae1b3863fd71fd4ee33acb3d58f8a062b55b) and Wn8030.h
    Taken into Wn8030Piano.h: the boot ROM protocol (commands, states, id 0xc8), the image check and the header/data block layout,
    the command frame and its checksum, the vendor message kinds, the design of the touchpad-as-pointer conversion
    (wn8030_pointer_report: one finger moves, two scroll, no jump when fingers change, palms lifted) and the command codes.
    Changed for piano: runtime commands to register 0x4c, piano's packed frames, the 27-byte touchpad report with 8-byte fingers,
    the attach bit (byte 9 bit 0), the consumer report's 5 bytes; taps added.
  package/KeyboardCover.cpp (sha256 35cdacf115e4599d7195ec52d8419f93520b595f09df8058cb34cc05cfb2e843)
    Facts: macOS 27 makes no pointer of a touchpad's finger collections, so a relative pointer; the Caps Lock output report path.
  package/KeyboardProbe.cpp (sha256 c98c61c12819611359bcc656f1b5830e9f21d5fb238845732ae31d372832d3a5)
    The bring-up order (pins, supplies, power-on, image, serving), the attach handling and the 12 s keyboard-power keepalive,
    authentication left unanswered. Not taken: its GENI engine and interrupt plumbing (sheng's kernel, not a kext).

Project-SunUEFI (unixnu-research/Project-SunUEFI, main 4ef87402e9d58465af871e4c4f4a5de87599d81c), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  uefi/components/pogo-product/PianoPogoBoard.c (sha256 7739d3b85d25b6028d22d425e4b7496e56ffaf8191b07a1b9efea11ad9c88b85),
  PianoPogoMcu.c (sha256 290e0e1bb3f488c73bffe1db90679aed50fd93c4020b70cd6e082bbd2e6ae296), PianoPogoService.c
  (sha256 8a8950d587a5ddbe258c6d88566f1a9815d5efc73e086c76ed26ec99a9b6976d)
    piano's facts: SDA/SCL gpio56/57, reset gpio188, sleep gpio3, irq gpio97 (rising-edge latch with INTR_CFG target at bits 10:8,
    raw status, enable off), the eGPIO claim, rails ldob11 1.8 V before ldob14 3.3 V (voltage, enable, mode 7), the timing (reset
    2 ms, boot ROM 500 ms, wake 50 ms, 3 ms after every boot ROM write), runtime register 0x4c. Not verified on hardware there.

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoInput (PianoHIDDevice, itself DroidVMInput's DroidVMHIDDevice from macOS-DroidVM overlay/kext/DroidVMInput,
    sha256 f05d9d9912b1ae5b57000dcc49f6a4539410e5212c34b31aa4270e31cfac8afc): the IOHIDDevice subclass and how it is published
    (OSTypeAlloc, init, attach, start under the service), the event-service notification, the codeless IOHIDEventDriver personality
    and the vtable check of tooling/k27/kext/PianoKeyboard.json. Same overrides plus setReport (the LED output report).
  package/PianoPower/Gauge.h: the software I2C bus (generalised in BitI2c.h: writes, repeated-START reads, a configurable clock).
  package/PianoPower/QcomRpmh.c and PianoAdsp.cpp: the cmd-db lookup and the RSC layouts (CmdDb.h), the active TCS vote sequence
    (PianoKeyboard.cpp voteLocked()), the apps RSC and cmd-db addresses, and (f53192b) how a vote holds the DRV-2 lock.
  package/PianoA830/adreno830/platform/sm8750/Sm8750Rpmh.h ("DRV-2 lock"): the owner word sm8750_rpmh_drv2_owner and its protocol
    (compare-exchange 0 for a tag, 10 us between tries, at most 2 s, store 0), used by PianoKeyboard.cpp vote() with the tag 'KBRD'.

Read as a specification only, never copied (GPL-2.0): Linux hid-nanosic-wn8030 (blu-sharky/linux-piano, map220v, GPL-2.0-only), as
built in the v1.1.0 Ubuntu release (debs/linux-image-7.2.15-piano58_7.2.15-58.1_arm64.deb, sha256
53b55b325519be948a598d0a929d2003341439ef157ec556097e03d825a352b7; drivers/hid/hid-nanosic-wn8030.ko sha256
8434ebe582b1abc52c57146fb049c7340d0ca9a7cc2ef0b2bd56a4b2682f5d28): the piano frame packing and report sizes, the runtime command
register, the attach bit, the touchpad device made on the first 0x19 report, the commands sent on attach, and the report layouts as
its piano HID descriptors declare them; 2026-11-11 also the frame check (type 0x39/0x4a/0x5b/0x6c), the attach bit (byte 9 bit 0,
tablet mode its inverse), the keyboard and consumer reports passed through (3 consumer bytes), the touchpad device on the first 0x19
report and the mouse reports dropped after it, the auth kinds and lengths. Also read as a specification only (GPL-2.0), the newer
port with the touchpad made at attach, as embedded in Project-SunUEFI patches/linux/7.3/0003-input-wireless.patch (sha256
b3cb4f645a654c94886e7c6101697c346ff70879edc8b741069eb1b3653fdf0d) and its follow-ups 0024/0037/0074 there: the touchpad HID
descriptor's physical size (94 x 42 mm: the 2/3 Y scale of Wn8030Piano.h's Pointer), the Windows-8 digitizer layout (contact count,
hid-multitouch's reading of it), the touchpad enable as the only touchpad command (no feature-report transport), the Right Ctrl
function row (the opt-in Keys::fnRow, written fresh from that behaviour), 0x24's request values, the hall (SW_LID) handling that
turns input off while closed (not done here). Linux's HID core (hid-input, ErrorRollOver ignored in a keyboard array): the rollover
rule of Keys. The macOS descriptors (HidDescriptors.h) are written from the HID 1.11 specification and the HID Usage Tables.

Facts from piano itself: the 2026-11-11 capture (logs/usb-console/20261111-084701-port0.txt, not committed): frame trailer = byte
sum of bytes 2..66, each vendor message's own sum, the ack (kind 0xf0) and state messages after each command, kinds 0xa4/0x28/0x01.
piano's boot DT (v1.1.0 piano-boot.dtb, sha256 50636effb5f54306ec0ab9a3061cd163d7f003d8797e04585a33205918856840): gpio-keys
switch-lid on TLMM gpio80, EV_SW/SW_LID, GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW (the hall sensor).

Read as a reference only (Apple Public Source License; nothing copied): IOHIDFamily as fetched by UniXNU
(unixnu-research/UniXNU/out/feeds/IOHIDFamily-f53ac321): IOHIDEventService::determineResolution and its defaults (400 dpi, 9 for
scrolling), IOHIDEventDriver::handleScrollReport (whole Wheel / AC Pan counts, AC Pan negated, no Resolution Multiplier), the HID
event system's pointer and scroll accelerators (IOHIDPointerScrollFilter, IOHIDAcceleration*: resolution-normalised): the facts
behind HidDescriptors.h's makeTouchpadDescriptor and the Pointer defaults. Behaviour only, from libinput's documentation (MIT):
disable-while-typing and tap button mapping (one, two, three fingers: left, right, middle), as the typing guard and the taps.

The MCU image (MCU_Upgrade.bin, stock OS3.0.303.0 odm_a, 83,436 bytes, sha256
c03d6b650cb85a983359c6686d831875df10ee1206fd31afc1403baefeb7e407) is Xiaomi/Nanosic's and is never committed: the build copies the
pinned file into the ignored out/native-kexts/PianoKeyboard/firmware and embeds it from there.
